## A3 — Pollution/growth comparison sign

### Joint verdict

The mathematical inequality is clear:

\[
g_K\le0,
\quad K\le K_{max}
\Longrightarrow
 g(S,K)\ge g(S,K_{max}).
\]

The direction of the kernel bound depends on whether \(g\) is a beneficial growth/regeneration term or a harmful generation term.

### Source-specific adjudication

In Article 001 the relevant \(g(S,K)\) is pollution-suppressed **growth**, so the \(K_{max}\)-frozen system is pessimistic and yields an inner bound, provided the sink constraint is invariant. The source prose sign should be corrected; the inner-bound conclusion can survive.

### Status

Conditional theorem after proof correction.

