## A7 — Commons obstruction

### Joint verdict

**Consensus: model/definition incomplete.**

### Canonical repair

Define the pointwise safe-harvest capacity through the tangent condition or state a direct drift certificate. A robust finite-time obstruction is:

\[
\dot S
=g(S)-H^{NE}(S)
\le-\varepsilon
\]

on the full safe interval or on a boundary strip that every relevant trajectory is proved to reach.

Negative drift without a uniform margin does not imply finite-time exit; \(\dot S=-S^2\) at floor zero is the standard counterexample.

### Status

Definition plus conditional obstruction theorem.

