## C1 — Epistemic fixed-point operator

### Joint verdict

The source presentation is flawed, but the two recursive forms can generate the same descending chain under monotone \(Pre\) when initialized at the safe top set.

### Canonical choice

Use

\[
\Phi(Q)
=S_{safe}\cap Pre(Q),
\qquad Q_0=S_{safe}.
\]

This is the official monotone Tarski operator.

The deflationary form

\[
Q\cap Pre(Q)
\]

may be used only as an implementation of the same descending chain after equivalence is proved for the chosen initialization.

### Countable versus transfinite

Countable intersection is justified in finite models and in compact/closed constructions where predecessor commutes with nested intersections and nested action witnesses have nonempty compact intersection. In a general powerset lattice, transfinite iteration may be required.

### Reviewer-side corrections

- ER001’s statement that \(Q\cap Pre(Q)\) is not monotone is false when \(Pre\) is monotone.
- Exact ordinal bounds proposed by reviewers are not adopted.
- The safe-base form is retained because it prevents computation of an invariant but unsafe set when initialized incorrectly.

### Status

Replace Article 006 theorem. Article 001/002 restricted constructions remain canonical.

